Added `accept_string_booleans`, a per-provider switch for a provider that sends `email_verified` as the string `"true"` rather than as a boolean, as Oracle Access Manager and some Keycloak configurations do. Against such a provider every address silently arrived unverified. Only `"true"` and `"false"` are read; `1` and `yes` are still refused, and the strict comparison every gate makes is unchanged. @ericof
